Input: goodix - poll at 60fps when no touch INT line is wired

Port of the sibling luckfox-yocto (RK3506) goodix poll fallback to the
starfive 6.12 vendor tree. The 10.1-DSI-TOUCH-A panel reaches the VF2 via a
22-pin -> 15-pin RPi-DSI converter that routes no touch-INT line, so the
GT9271 probes (ID/version read OK over I2C) but request_threaded_irq fails
(gpiod_to_irq(NULL) -> -EINVAL) and the driver never binds. When no int-gpio
is present, drive the controller with a 17 ms (60 fps) i2c poll timer instead
of an interrupt; the touchscreen DT node then needs only compatible + reg.

Differs from the RK3506 original only in the branch condition: this vendor
tree derives the IRQ from gpiod_to_irq(ts->gpiod_int) rather than
client->irq, so branch on ts->gpiod_int.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [vendor poll fallback for board with no touch IRQ]

